  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.0.11 - A Blazor / WebAssembly app no longer gets CA1416 warnings for calling SpawnJS (the app assembly is marked browser-only; opt out: SpawnJSSupportedPlatformAttribute=false). v3.0.10 - FIX (trimmed apps): an options / dictionary class of the wrapper namespaces that this library never names at a call site (EcKeyImportParams passed to SubtleCrypto.ImportKey through a Union of its base) lost its property getters in a trimmed publish and failed with ArgumentException: Arg_GetMethNotFnd (3.0.9 only). The trim descriptor keeps their accessors again (+18 KB). v3.0.9 - WebAuthn JSON: PublicKeyCredential.ParseCreationOptionsFromJSON / ParseRequestOptionsFromJSON, ToJSON / ToJSONString, CredentialsContainer Create / Get overloads for the parsed options (passkeys with any server speaking the standard base64url JSON). Trimmed apps about 650 KB smaller: the embedded trim descriptor keeps only wrapper constructors (was every member). v3.0.8 - DisplayMediaStreamOptions.WindowAudio (exclude / system / window: which audio a window capture offers). WebCodecs chunk types and GainNodeOptions channel options cross to Javascript as strings (EnumString). v3.0.7 - Fixed: MediaDevices.GetUserMedia(bool video, bool audio) opened no camera or microphone in a trimmed app (it sent an anonymous object, which arrived as {}). Full history: CHANGELOG.md",
